{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775378800-1ezbQJSskOxOANtv76Pa","role":"assistant","created":1775378818,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data I need. Let me extract the Social Security Administration nominal budget outlay data from each December Treasury Bulletin:\n\nFrom the FFO-4 tables, I need to find the \"Social Security Administration\" row and get the \"Total funds\" column (column 4) which represents the current fiscal year to date.\n\nLet me parse out the data:\n\n1. December 2011 Treasury Bulletin (for FY2011 - but wait, I need data from FY2010 to FY2019. The December 2011 bulletin would give data for FY2011 and the prior year FY2010)\n\nActually wait, let me re-read the problem. It says \"U.S. Federal Social Security Administration nominal budget outlay from FY2010 to FY2019\". And it says to use FFO-4 tables in December Treasury Bulletins from odd years between 2010 and 2019.\n\nSo I need to use:\n- December 2011 Treasury Bulletin → gives FY2011 and FY2010 data (current FY and prior FY)\n- December 2013 Treasury Bulletin → gives FY2013 and FY2012 data\n- December 2015 Treasury Bulletin → gives FY2015 and FY2014 data\n- December 2017 Treasury Bulletin → gives FY2017 and FY2016 data\n- December 2019 Treasury Bulletin → gives FY2019 and FY2018 data\n\nWait, but I only have data from odd years. Let me think again...\n\nActually, looking at the tables more carefully:\n- December 2011: Shows \"This fiscal year to date\" = FY2011 and \"Prior fiscal year to date\" = FY2010\n- December 2013: Shows \"This fiscal year to date\" = FY2013 and \"Prior fiscal year to date\" = FY2012\n- December 2015: Shows \"This fiscal year to date\" = FY2015 and \"Prior fiscal year to date\" = FY2014\n\n\n- December 2017: Shows \"This fiscal year to date\" = FY2017 and \"Prior fiscal year to date\" = FY2016\n- December 2019: Shows \"This fiscal year to date\" = FY2019 and \"Prior fiscal year to date\" = FY2018\n\nI'll need to strategically select the \"This fiscal year to date\" data from each December Treasury Bulletin to cover the entire range from FY2010 to FY2019. This means pulling the current year data from each odd-year bulletin will give me a comprehensive view of the Social Security Administration's nominal budget outlays.\n\nI'll extract the total funds for Social Security Administration from each document:\n- FY2011: $784,194 million (December 2011)\n- FY2013: $867,394 million (December 2013)\n- FY2015: $944,143 million (December 2015)\n- FY2017: $1,000,812 million (December 2017)\n- FY2019: $1,101,833 million (December 2019)\n\nThe problem specifically requests using FFO-4 tables from December Treasury Bulletins in odd years between 2010 and 2019. I'm realizing I need to clarify which fiscal years' data these bulletins actually represent.\n\nEach December Treasury Bulletin for odd years provides data for two fiscal years: the current fiscal year and the prior fiscal year. This means I'll need to extract specific year data from different bulletins to cover the full range from FY2010 to FY2019.\n\nThe key is to identify the correct fiscal year data within each bulletin, ensuring I'm capturing the precise information needed for the analysis.\n\nI'll carefully select the appropriate fiscal year totals from each bulletin, noting that the \"This fiscal year to date\" column represents the current fiscal year's data at that specific point in time.\n\nI'll compile the SSA outlay data across the odd-numbered fiscal years from 2011 to 2019, using the \"Total funds\" column from each Treasury Bulletin. The sequence will include the outlays for FY2011, FY2013, FY2015, FY2017, and FY2019, which correspond to the specified years in the task.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_ed3bb60085b646c5a04888d0","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport math\n\n# SSA Outlay data from FFO-4 tables (in millions)\n# From December Treasury Bulletins:\n# Dec 2011: FY2011 = 784,194 ; FY2010 (prior) = 754,179\n# Dec 2013: FY2013 = 867,394 ; FY2012 (prior) = 821,144\n# Dec 2015: FY2015 = 944,143 ; FY2014 (prior) = 905,769\n# Dec 2017: FY2017 = 1,000,812 ; FY2016 (prior) = 976,783\n# Dec 2019: FY2019 = 1,101,833 ; FY2018 (prior) = 1,039,902\n\n# Data points for FY2010 to FY2019 (10 years)\ndata = [\n    754179,  # FY2010 (from Dec 2011 bulletin - prior year)\n    784194,  # FY2011 (from Dec 2011 bulletin)\n    821144,  # FY2012 (from Dec 2013 bulletin - prior year)\n    867394,  # FY2013 (from Dec 2013 bulletin)\n    905769,  # FY2014 (from Dec 2015 bulletin - prior year)\n    944143,  # FY2015 (from Dec 2015 bulletin)\n    976783,  # FY2016 (from Dec 2017 bulletin - prior year)\n    1000812, # FY2017 (from Dec 2017 bulletin)\n    1039902, # FY2018 (from Dec 2019 bulletin - prior year)\n    1101833, # FY2019 (from Dec 2019 bulletin)\n]\n\nprint(\"SSA Outlays (in millions):\")\nfor i, val in enumerate(data, 2010):\n    print(f\"FY{i}: {val:,}\")\n\n# Calculate mean\nn = len(data)\nmean = sum(data) / n\nprint(f\"\\nMean: {mean:,.2f}\")\n\n# Calculate population standard deviation\n# For population std dev, we divide by N (not N-1)\nvariance = sum((x - mean) ** 2 for x in data) / n\npop_std = math.sqrt(variance)\nprint(f\"Population Standard Deviation: {pop_std:,.2f}\")\n\n# Calculate coefficient of variation\ncv = (pop_std / mean) * 100\nprint(f\"\\nCoefficient of Variation: {cv:.4f}%\")\nprint(f\"Rounded to nearest hundredths: {cv:.2f}%\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
